## Test Anti-Pattern Audit — Severity-Ranked Findings

This is a textbook **"coverage theater"** suite. Every production method is invoked (hence 95% coverage), but almost nothing is actually verified. Here are the findings, ranked by production-bug risk:

---

### 🔴 CRITICAL — Missing Assertions (fire-and-forget tests)

**1. `AddProduct_Works` (line 17)** — No assertion at all. The product could silently fail to persist.
```csharp
// FIX: verify the product was actually stored
_catalog.AddProduct(product);
var stored = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNotNull(stored);
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", stored.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, stored.Price);
```

**2. `UpdatePrice_Works` (line 31)** — Calls `UpdatePrice` but never checks the price changed. A no-op `Save` would pass this test.
```csharp
// FIX: assert the new price is persisted
_catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);
var updated = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, updated!.Price);
```

**3. `RemoveProduct_Works` (line 37)** — Calls `RemoveProduct` but never verifies the product is gone. Delete could be a no-op.
```csharp
// FIX: assert product no longer exists
_catalog.RemoveProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNull(_catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001"));
```

**4. `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` (line 68)** — Applies a 10% discount to two products, checks nothing. A broken discount formula (e.g. `Price * fraction` instead of `Price * (1 - fraction)`) would pass.
```csharp
// FIX: verify computed prices
_catalog.ApplyBulkDiscount(0.10m);
Assert.AreEqual(8.991m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001")!.Price);
Assert.AreEqual(17.991m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-002")!.Price);
```

**5. `GetProductCount_Works` (line 63)** — Never asserts the count value. Also tests on an *empty* catalog, so the method is exercised in a trivial, meaningless state.
```csharp
// FIX: assert against a known count
_catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
_catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-002", "Gadget", 19.99m));
Assert.AreEqual(2, _catalog.GetProductCount());
```

**6. `ImportFromCsv_Works` (line 84)** — Imports a CSV line, never checks a product was created. Parsing bugs would be invisible.
```csharp
// FIX: verify the imported product
_catalog.ImportFromCsv("SKU-001,Widget,9.99");
var p = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNotNull(p);
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", p.Name);
